<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Model fidelity to source: 91/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Solves the exact Thomas (1975) / Murray (1981) steady state (u0, v0) = (9.9338, 9.2892), Jacobian, d_c = 9.6292 and dispersion curve (L169-259); counts Neumann cylinder eigenmodes from n = 0 and distinguishes r_crit = 0.7527 (fastest mode) from the full-exclusion radius r_excl = 1/k_+ = 0.36 (L264-338, Lean Theorem 5); integrates the tapered tail with a fully implicit per-Fourier-mode surface Laplace-Beltrami operator including the arc-length metric factor (L340-470), replacing the v2 explicit-axial scheme that violated its own stability limit; runs the planar PDE to saturation with a genuine two-stage protocol (L475-563); and assembles a P1 cotangent surface FEM (L697-789) whose m = 1 cylinder eigenvalue matches the analytic value to 3.1e-14 and whose stiffness rows sum to zero (Lean Theorem 4), on which the two-stage run is executed on the felid body (L955-1056). Not 94 as in v2: the body is a surface of revolution rather than a scanned mesh, the FEM reaction step is explicit (dt = 0.1 is only safe because |eig J0| <= 7.1 at Table 1; the K = 0 control needs dt = 0.02), and the demonstration tail had to be thinned to r_tip = 0.15 for the ring zone to exist -- the v2 geometry does not produce rings." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-model-fidelity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/model-fidelity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py L20–L34: Disclosure that the v2 conical solver was numerically unstable (dt = 0.015 > 0.0043) and that its 865x ratio was a clipping artifact <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L20-L34>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-3>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-4>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-5>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-6>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-model-fidelity-7> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9.1e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-morphometric-validation> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Morphometric validation: 84/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "`measure_morphoeval()` (L1513-1676) now emits 14 measurements: the four exact analytic quantities (u0, d_c, gamma*k_c^2, r_crit; error 0), the gamma-vs-mode-count Pearson r = 0.9996, both negative controls (std_u 8.6e-15 and 4.1e-16), the specimen Delaunay CV (0.296 vs 0.24), the FEM m = 1 eigenvalue error (3.1e-14), the FEM tail ring onset (0.817 measured vs 0.858 predicted from r_excl), the FEM torso annularity (0.84 vs planar 0.80), the G = 1 null (0.0) and the FEM marking density (5.09 vs 18.9). It also RETRACTS the v2 headline: the conical suppression ratio on the v2 geometry is 0.90, not 865.5, and this is carried as an explicit disclosure measurement (L1636-1647); the new ratio (9.86 vs reference 5.0) is on a thinner tail chosen so that r_excl is reached. Weaknesses: the annularity reference (0.8) is the script's own planar run, not a literature value; the ring-onset reference is linear theory on a surrogate taper; the marking-density measurement fails by 3.7x; and no measurement uses segmented rosette morphology from the specimen." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-morphometric-validation> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/morphometric-validation" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py L1636–L1647: v2 865x suppression ratio retracted: stable solver on the v2 geometry gives 0.90 (no exclusion zone) <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L1636-L1647>",
        "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py L565–L592: Annularity index (rim-vs-core of Stage-1 cores in the Stage-2 field) -- a self-defined statistic, not a literature morphometric <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L565-L592>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-conical-tail-critical-circumferential-cutoff-radius-r-crit-m-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-conical-tail-pde-proximal-to-distal-circumferential-spot-suppression-ratio>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-conical-tail-pde-suppression-ratio-on-the-v2-geometry-r-tip-0-35-r-excl-v2-artifact-disclosure>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-equal-diffusion-d-1-and-non-inhibitory-k-0-negative-control-amplitude-suppression>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-fem-felid-body-tail-spot-to-ring-transition-position-measured-vs-full-exclusion-prediction-r-excl-1-k>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-fem-stage-2-torso-markings-per-torso-depth-vs-specimen-estimate>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-p1-surface-fem-laplace-beltrami-m-1-cylinder-eigenvalue-relative-error>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-scale-factor-gamma-vs-unstable-eigenmode-count-pearson-r>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-segmented-panthera-pardus-kruger-flank-inter-rosette-delaunay-wavelength-cv>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-thomas-critical-diffusivity-ratio-d-c>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-thomas-steady-state-substrate-concentration-u0>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-turing-critical-wavenumber-squared-gamma-k-c-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-two-stage-annularity-index-with-no-growth-g-1-null-control-planar>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-measurement-two-stage-stage-2-annularity-index-on-the-fem-torso-at-growth-factor-g-2>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-morphometric-validation-1> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.4e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-overall> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — MorphoEval overall 84.2/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Pass 3 (v3) post-remediation evaluation of `1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py` (overall weighted score: 84.2 / 100, DOWN 7.4 points from 91.6 / 100 in Pass 2, up from 49.4 / 100 in Pass 1). The v3 script keeps the exact Thomas (1975) / Murray (1981) steady state, Jacobian, d_c and dispersion analysis; replaces the numerically unstable v2 conical-tail solver with a fully implicit surface-of-revolution Laplace-Beltrami solver (metric factor 1/(1+r'^2) included) and shows that the v2 geometry has no ring zone; adds a P1 cotangent surface finite-element solver on a triangulated 3D felid body of revolution (47,520 vertices) verified against the exact cylinder spectrum, on which the Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006) two-stage protocol is run as a genuine PDE (cub body -> adult body, growth factor G = 2) yielding torso annularity 0.84 and a tail ring onset at x/L_tail = 0.82 vs the Lean-backed prediction 0.86; sweeps G in {1, 1.5, 2, 3} on the planar flank; and backs five mathematical laws with machine-checked Lean 4 theorems (0 sorrys). The score falls because v3 retracts the v2 865x suppression ratio (clipping artifact), shows the v2 \"two-stage\" step to have been an image filter on a linear-regime field, finds the specimen tail ROI mis-placed, reports a 3.7x marking-density shortfall against the specimen (5.1 vs 18.9 markings per torso depth), and finds the kinetic CLI flags unwired -- none of which v2 had penalised. Overall 84.2/100 (faithfulness 81.1, reproducibility 91.2); rubric morphoeval 0.1.0; checkpoint commit 64526a0; environment: python 3.14.7, numpy 2.4.2, scipy 1.17.0, matplotlib 3.10.8, Pillow 12.1.1. Dimension assessments: Model fidelity to source 91, Morphological realism / specimen match 72, Parameter expressivity 80, Morphometric validation 84, Source and data traceability 92, Code-to-model traceability 92, Reproducibility package 90. Output judged: docs/media/mammalian_coat_markings_comparison.png: rendered output of 1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py at 64526a0, image/png, 1273921 B, 2366×1881 px, artifact_sha256 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a (sha256 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a), spec_fingerprint b990576b2a4b3ccd36c08d1a21625f5ebd87766fc673675eaee0d8216821ffd3. Dual provenance: spec_fingerprint: b990576b2a4b3ccd36c08d1a21625f5ebd87766fc673675eaee0d8216821ffd3; artifact_sha256: 417dee8b24b004962c52143eefd329402da37f468ef4c9cbd844a2d13282558a; input_dataset_sha256: {datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json=65978462afc1b9e7..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/mammalian_coat_markings_reference.json=24d56069831e0ee9..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/panthera_pardus_specimen.jpg=86533a5dcf9cfee6..., datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/scout_manifest.json=28eabc9cf247b03e...}. Supersedes audit: 2026-10-19-mammalian-coat-markings-audit-v2. Claim boundary: reported_in_source: Murray (1981): Thomas substrate-inhibition kinetics at a = 92, b = 64, alpha = 1.5, rho = 18.5, K = 0.1 are diffusively unstable for d > d_c; the domain scale factor gamma selects between no pattern, stripes, spots and crowding; on a tapered cylinder spot modes (m >= 1) are excluded below a critical radius so a spotted animal can have a ringed tail but not vice versa | Liu, Liaw & Maini (2006): leopard rosettes arise from a two-stage process in which a juvenile spot pre-pattern is re-run under changed parameters on the grown adult skin | Dziuk (1988), Pinkall & Polthier (1993), Dziuk & Elliott (2013): P1 surface finite elements with cotangent weights converge to the Laplace-Beltrami operator on a triangulated surface; reconstructed_in_script: Exact steady state, Jacobian, d_c, dispersion curve and Turing band; Neumann cylinder eigenmode counting including n = 0; r_crit (fastest-mode) and r_excl = 1/k_+ (full-exclusion) radii; fully implicit conical-tail PDE; planar DCT-II IMEX PDE run to saturation with a genuine two-stage protocol and growth-factor sweep; P1 surface FEM (stiffness/mass assembly, spectrum verification, two-stage run on the felid body) with annularity and spot-spacing diagnostics; DoG segmentation of the Kruger specimen; transfer_boundary: The 3D body is a parametric surface of revolution with hand-set knots (felid_body_profile.json), not a photogrammetric scan; its head-body length of 22 cub wavelengths and the growth factor G = 2 are ASSUMED, not fitted, which is why the FEM marking density (5.1 per torso depth) is 3.7x below the specimen estimate (18.9) | The tail ring onset comparison (0.82 measured vs 0.86 predicted) is on the surrogate taper, whose tip radius (0.004 HBL) was chosen to lie below r_excl; it is a consistency check of solver against linear theory, not a measurement on a real tail | The specimen is a 3/4-view photograph: the flank ROI is foreshortened and the v2 tail ROI covers hindquarters/background, so the Delaunay CV and polygonality are flank-only statistics; does_not_claim: That Murray (1981) or Liu et al. (2006) reported any of the FEM, annularity, growth-sweep or marking-density numbers; all are v3 reconstructions | That the Thomas kinetics are the biological mechanism of felid pigmentation." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-rubric-0.1.0> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/overall" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "remediation needed: Add the surface-FEM and body-proportion references (Dziuk 1988, Pinkall & Polthier 1993, Dziuk & Elliott 2013, Stein & Hayssen 2013) to `datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/paper_citations.bib` and re-pin its SHA-256 in `EXPECTED_SHA256` (L128-130).",
        "remediation needed: Fit the body scale and growth factor to the specimen instead of assuming them: HBL = 22 lambda_c and G = 2 give 5.09 markings per torso depth vs 18.9 observed (`run_two_stage_fem_body`, L1025-1053; measurement 'FEM Stage-2 torso markings per torso depth', L1573-1581). Sweep HBL/lambda_c in [22, 90] and G in [1.5, 3] and report the (HBL, G) that matches the specimen density and polygonality jointly.",
        "remediation needed: Make the initial noise field mesh-resolution independent (`integrate_thomas_fem_surface_pde` L870-876 draws per-vertex noise; planar reseed at L544), e.g. by projecting a fixed low-pass random field onto the mesh, so that the FEM spot layout is reproducible across `nx`/`ntheta` and the coarse self-test body (nx = 200) and the default render (nx = 360) seed the same pattern.",
        "remediation needed: Relocate the specimen tail ROI onto the curled tail (approximately x = 470-530, y = 200-240 per `felid_body_profile.json` L64) or replace the 3/4-view specimen with a lateral-view, SHA-pinned photograph in which the tail is resolved, then add a measured tail spot-to-ring onset to compare with `tail_exclusion_fraction` (currently only the surrogate-mesh value is compared, L1543-1551).",
        "remediation needed: Replace the parametric surface of revolution with a triangulated photogrammetric or CT-derived felid body mesh (`build_felid_body_surface_mesh`, L791-834; profile knots at `datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json` L44-48): the FEM assembly (`assemble_p1_fem_laplace_beltrami`, L721-753) is already mesh-agnostic, so this is a data item, not a solver item. Carried over from v2 in reduced form.",
        "remediation needed: Wire the kinetic and scale CLI flags into the solvers: `--a`, `--b`, `--alpha`, `--rho`, `--K`, `--d`, `--gamma`, `--steps`, `--seed` are parsed at L1783-1791 but `render_outputs()` is called with `growth_factor` only (L1800); thread a parameter dict through `compute_thomas_steady_state`, `integrate_thomas_pde_2d`, `integrate_thomas_conical_tail_pde` and `run_two_stage_fem_body`, and add a self-test check that `--K 0` reproduces the negative control." ;
    pk1:hasScore 8.42e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-parameter-expressivity> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Parameter expressivity: 80/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Sweeps Murray's five gamma regimes {0.4, 3.5, 8, 25, 120} to saturation (`run_scale_morphospace_sweep`, L620-668), runs dual negative controls at d = 1 and K = 0 with the stability-appropriate time step (L671-692), adds a Liu-Liaw-Maini growth-factor sweep G in {1, 1.5, 2, 3} with an annularity read-out (L594-618, Panel K; non-monotonic: G = 3 yields central-spot jaguar-like rosettes, annularity 0.25), and exposes `--growth-factor`, which IS wired through to both the planar and FEM two-stage runs (L1792, L1800). However the kinetic/scale flags `--a`, `--b`, `--alpha`, `--rho`, `--K`, `--d`, `--gamma`, `--seed` and `--steps` are parsed (L1783-1791) and never passed to any solver: `render_outputs` is called with `growth_factor` only (L1800). v2 scored this dimension 90 on the strength of \"full CLI flags\" that were already inert in v2." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-parameter-expressivity> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/parameter-expressivity" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py L1783–L1800: CLI parses a, b, alpha, rho, K, d, gamma, steps, seed but only growth_factor reaches render_outputs() <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L1783-L1800>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-parameter-expressivity-1> ;
    pk1:hasScore 8e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-repro-package> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Reproducibility package: 90/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Deterministic RNG (`seed=1981`), a 12-check `--self-test` (L1681-1778) covering SHA locks, JSON parity, the K*u0^2 > 1 threshold, the n = 0-inclusive mode census, the stable conical solver (ring zone exists at r_tip = 0.15 and does NOT at the v2 r_tip = 0.35, field stays off the clip bounds), both controls, segmentation, bitwise two-run determinism, FEM cylinder spectrum, FEM mass conservation, a coarse FEM body run and the G = 1 <= G = 2 annularity ordering; three self-contained outputs (12-panel PNG, FEM-surface PNG, 12-frame GIF). Render ~55-70 s and self-test ~70 s on the reference machine. Residual: the initial noise amplitude is applied per vertex, so the seeded field (and hence the exact spot layout) depends on mesh resolution." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-repro-package> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/repro-package" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-repro-package-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-repro-package-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 9e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "faithful" .

<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-source-traceability> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Source and data traceability: 92/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "Vendors `datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/` with the reference JSON, the specimen photograph, the scout manifest, `paper_citations.bib` and the new `felid_body_profile.json` (knots, growth defaults, specimen scale estimates, Stein et al. 2013 proportion sources, honesty statement), all five files SHA-256-verified at runtime (`EXPECTED_SHA256`, L118-134; `verify_dataset_sha256`, L140-152). The four surface-FEM references (Dziuk 1988, Pinkall & Polthier 1993, Dziuk & Elliott 2013, Stein & Hayssen 2013) are cited with DOIs in the module docstring and this audit but are NOT in `paper_citations.bib`, which is SHA-pinned and was left untouched." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-source-traceability> ;
