<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/assessment/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-specimen-match> a pk1:LLMClaimAssessment ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Thomas substrate-inhibition reaction-diffusion pre-pattern, conical tail spot-to-ring transition & P1 surface-FEM felid body — Morphological realism / specimen match: 72/100" ;
    dct:date "2026-10-20"^^xsd:date ;
    dct:description "The SHA-256-locked Kruger *Panthera pardus pardus* photograph is loaded and segmented into N = 164 flank markings (DoG + opening, L1082-1155) with Delaunay NN spacing 7.44 px (CV 0.30) and interior Voronoi polygonality compared against the planar PDE lattice (Panels E, F, H); the FEM body now yields a marking density that can be compared with the specimen. But that comparison FAILS by 3.7x (FEM Stage 2: 5.1 markings per torso depth vs specimen estimate 18.9, `felid_body_profile.json` L63) because HBL = 22 lambda_c and G = 2 are assumed, not fitted; the v2 tail ROI [410, 115, 560, 225] covers mostly hindquarters and background grass on this 3/4-view image (caveat recorded at `felid_body_profile.json` L64) so no tail statistic is actually measured on the animal; and the FEM \"rosettes\" are compared to the specimen only through a self-defined annularity index, not through segmented rosette morphology (ring/core ratios, rosette diameters). v2's 89 credited a tail ROI that does not contain the tail." ;
    dct:subject <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/concept/morphoeval-0.1.0-specimen-match> ;
    pk1:assessedBy <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/model/gemini-4-argon> ;
    pk1:assessmentType "morphoeval/0.1.0/specimen-match" ;
    pk1:evidenceAgainst "1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py L1025–L1053: FEM markings-per-torso-depth computed and compared with the specimen estimate (5.09 vs 18.9) -- the comparison is made but the model is 3.7x too coarse <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L1025-L1053>",
        "datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json L57–L65: Specimen torso-depth scale estimate (18.9 markings per torso depth) and the tail-ROI caveat: the v2 tail ROI is on the hindquarters/background <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/datasets/mammalian_coat_markings/felid_body_profile.json#L57-L65>" ;
    pk1:hasEvidence <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-specimen-match-1>,
        <https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/evidence/morphoeval-murray-mammalian-coat-markings-specimen-match-2> ;
    pk1:hasScore 7.2e-01 ;
    pk1:hasVerdict "mostly faithful" .

