<https://w3id.org/probknow/resource/math-law/murray-mammalian-coat-markings-5> a skos:Concept,
        pk1:Concept ;
    rdfs:label "Murray (1981) Full Circumferential Exclusion Radius r_excl = 1/k_+ (n = 0 Longitudinal-Stripe Mode)" ;
    dct:description "Corrects the Pass 2 fastest-mode criterion r_crit (which only tests q_ax = k_c): between r_excl and r_crit a tail still carries long-axial-wavelength m ≥ 1 modes, so pure transverse rings appear only where the circumference 2πr drops below λ_+. Numerically twinned by the implicit conical solver (ring zone starts at x_excl/L) and the FEM body (tail_exclusion_fraction vs measured ring onset) | Variables: r(x): local tail radius; m: circumferential mode number; n = 0: axially uniform (Neumann-admissible) mode; k_+: upper edge of the unstable band; λ_+ = 2π/k_+: shortest unstable wavelength; r_excl: radius below which only m = 0 rings remain" ;
    dct:source "Murray (1981) J. Theor. Biol. 88(1):161-199 Section 4 Eqs. (26)-(32); Murray (1988) Sci. Am. 258(3):80-87" ;
    rdfs:seeAlso <https://github.com/fractastical/morpholib/blob/64526a0/1981-murray-mammalian-coat-markings.py#L255-L330>,
